**Director, Applied AI Engineering** **POSITION SUMMARY**
The Vector Institute is seeking a Director, Applied AI Engineering to help Canadian organizations adopt frontier AI safely, effectively, and at scale.


Reporting to the VP, AI Engineering, the Director leads Vector's technical engagements with industry sponsors, public sector organizations, startups, and strategic partners. They advise technical leaders on AI architecture and deployment, oversee practical engineering projects, and manage a small team of AI builders and technical advisors.


Working closely with Vector's AI Engineering Domain Leads, the Director translates emerging research and engineering advances into practical applications, reusable frameworks, and reference architectures that benefit Canada's AI ecosystem.

**KEY RESPONSIBILITIES*** Lead technical advisory and engineering engagements with sponsors, public sector organizations, Vector FastLane startups, and partners, ensuring technical excellence and practical value;
* Partner with the Vector Industry Innovation and Broader Public Sector teams to grow Vector’s industry sponsors and broader public sector partnerships, showcase research and technical expertise that Vector can offer to new partners, as well as develop and refine technical offerings from Vector;
* Advise technical leaders across the AI ecosystem on architecture, model selection, agentic systems, engineering patterns, evaluation, security, and deployment strategies;
* Stay on top of developments in frontier AI and offer timely educational sessions to Vector industry sponsors on the latest trends in AI with practical tips on how these trends impact business or technical practices;
* Set an annual strategy for high\-impact technical deliverables to support AI adoption across Vector industry sponsors, broader public sector partners, and startups, and track the successful execution of this strategy;
* Build a network of innovative AI CTOs and entrepreneurs in residence who can raise Vector’s impact and increase Vector’s reach to enable frontier AI adoption and best practices for our ecosystem;
* Lead and mentor a small team of AI builders and advisors maintaining high standards for AI engineering quality and delivery;
* Architect and oversee proofs of concept, prototypes, and targeted AI engineering projects addressing real\-world adoption challenges;
* Connect Vector's core AI Engineering domains with external partners, translating research and engineering advances into practical applications;
* Partner with the VP, AI Engineering and the Director of AI Engineering Portfolio \& Operations on technical scoping and delivery of prioritized engagements, ensuring adequate budget, compute, and staffing to deliver against core responsibilities;
* Represent Vector's technical expertise in industry sponsor discussions, workshops, executive briefings, and industry events;
* Develop reusable engineering frameworks, reference architectures, and implementation patterns addressing common industry challenges;
* Share insights from industry engagements with AI Engineering Product and Domain Leads to inform open\-source development and engineering roadmaps;
* Lead technical enablement for startup cohorts, advise startups and mentor Machine Learning Associates to deliver high\-quality solutions;
* Identify opportunities to develop open\-source tools addressing recurring needs across industry sponsor and startup engagements; and,
* Other related duties as assigned from time to time.

**KEY SUCCESS MEASURES*** Strong partner feedback on the quality and practical value of Vector's technical advisory and engineering engagements;
* Publication of reusable engineering frameworks, reference architectures, and implementation patterns applicable across organizations;
* Demonstrable progress by partners in validating AI use cases and advancing solutions toward production;
* Successful startup cohort delivery, including at least one open\-source tool annually addressing a significant market need;
* A high\-performing technical advisory team capable of independently delivering complex engagements; and,
* Actionable industry insights that inform Vector's product and engineering priorities.

 **PROFILE OF THE IDEAL CANDIDATE*** Bachelor's or master's degree in computer science, engineering, machine learning, or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience;
* 10\+ years in software engineering, architecture, or technical leadership, including 5\+ years leading complex initiatives or advising on critical technology decisions, with recent hands\-on production AI experience;
* Experience architecting AI systems, including LLM harnesses, agentic systems, evaluation frameworks, and production infrastructure;
* Strong engineering foundations, with the ability to evaluate designs, review code, guide implementation, and contribute to prototypes;
* Sound architectural judgment balancing emerging AI capabilities with reliability, security, cost, and business value;
* Experience advising organizations across different industries or technical environments, adapting recommendations to their needs and maturity;
* Excellent communication skills and credibility with engineering directors, architects, and technical executives;
* Experience leading and mentoring skilled AI technical talent, with strong delegation and technical quality standards; and,
* Commitment to applied AI research, open\-source engineering, and translating technical advances into reusable tools and practices.

 **TOTAL REWARDS:** The expected salary for this position will be $157,300 \- $196,600 per year, plus benefits if applicable. The final salary offer will reflect the successful candidate's experience, skills, and qualifications, in alignment with the Vector Institute's *Compensation Policy* and may differ from above.  

